{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>You now</b> Three times in the Masorah: here \"you now blessed of YHWH,\" and the others: \"you now shall make kingdom,\" \"you now are lightened from the yoke.\" Teaches that they made Isaac king over them, and this is \"you now shall make kingdom,\" and they lightened their yoke from upon you." "<b>Blessed of YHWH</b> Two times in the Masorah: here \"you now blessed of YHWH,\" and the other: \"come, blessed of YHWH.\" To say: just as the intent of Laban and Bethuel was to kill Eliezer as I explained, and \"they set [food] before him to eat,\" so too was the intent of Abimelech to kill Isaac. And thus the verse proves, as it is written \"since we did not touch you\" — meaning, we did not do evil to you as was in our mind, and we did with you only good."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:08.098308933Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}